Here is the edited program. I have added the necessary include for the math library (`<cmath>`) and used the `std::sqrt` function to calculate the square root. Note that since the input is an integer, the result will be cast to an integer, effectively truncating any decimal part.

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <cmath> // Required for std::sqrt

int main() 
{ 
    int number; 

    std::cout << "Enter an integer: "; 
    std::cin >> number; 

    // Calculate and print the square root
    // Casting to int truncates the decimal part
    int squareRoot = static_cast<int>(std::sqrt(number));

    std::cout << "The square root of " << number << " is " << squareRoot << std::endl;

    return 0;
}
```

